---
/*
 * CONTENT THAT STARTS HIDDEN, PARKED OUT OF THE DOCUMENT UNTIL ITS PANEL OPENS.
 *
 * Highlighted code is expensive in NODES rather than bytes. Measured on the built site, a component
 * page carried thousands of token spans that no reader could see on load: the Reference tab's
 * contract JSON (1,931 on `/components/button`, 5,376 on `/components/comment-thread`), the binding
 * half nobody picked (6,211), a source tab behind another one (3,912). All of it resolved styles and
 * took part in layout, and all of it is behind a click.
 *
 * A `<template>`'s content is an inert DocumentFragment: parsed, but not IN the document, so it
 * costs no style resolution, no layout and nothing to walk. `scripts/deferred-code.ts` clones it in
 * the moment the wrapper becomes visible, so the same markup arrives  -  unlike `CodeBlock`'s own
 * `full` density, which ships text and gives up highlighting to save the same nodes.
 *
 * ONLY FOR CONTENT HIDDEN AT LOAD. Something already visible gains nothing here and pays a clone;
 * the hydrator runs on first paint for anything visible, so wrapping a visible block is merely
 * wasteful rather than broken.
 *
 * THE WRAPPER IS A REAL BOX, not `display: contents`: the panel's own layout should be the same
 * whether the code has arrived yet or not, and a box that is empty for one frame is what makes the
 * hydration invisible.
 */
---

<div data-sk-deferred-code>
  <template data-sk-deferred-source><slot /></template>
</div>
